{
  "id": "T6b_effort",
  "title": "Repair effort per variant and block",
  "population": "REPAIR_CANDIDATES (diagnostic only; C02 also BASE, C05 FINAL[v] vs BASE)",
  "unit": "generation / repair request (see metric)",
  "notes": [
    "One row per effort estimate (all models); value = the estimate's point value (C01 per trajectory or per improved cell as given by its strata, C02 tokens per generation, C03 median seconds, C05 improved cells per effort unit); descriptive only, no ranking.",
    "Abbreviation in column Population: REPAIR_CAND. = REPAIR_CANDIDATES (the JSON form keeps the full name).",
    "BL01: Includes dense_la/00 (BL-01 tolerance convention: possible false FAIL verdicts; disclosure-bearing aggregate); sensitivity SA1 in T10.",
    "IC1: Q06 is in-sample for test_feedback and combined_feedback: their loops see the ParEval test verdict and stop when it passes (every stopped_tests_pass trajectory is a Q06 pass), so they optimise the endpoint; for static_feedback Q06 is out-of-sample (measured once in phase 2, never seen by the loop). The variants therefore differ in trigger and stop rules, not only in feedback content; test_feedback cannot regress on Q06 by construction.",
    "IC6: static_feedback repair triggers are dominated by clang-tidy bugprone findings and, on MPI, by low-confidence hints (design document: no trustworthy static MPI tool exists); static_feedback results measure this frozen blocking-set configuration, not static analysis in general."
  ],
  "definitions": [
    {
      "ref": "BASE",
      "text": "BASE: the 1,980 base cells (pilot_002 396 + full_ext_001 1,584), iteration-0 artifacts (use: initial code quality)"
    },
    {
      "ref": "REPAIR_CANDIDATES",
      "text": "REPAIR_CANDIDATES: the 3,480 repair candidates (iteration >= 1) (use: diagnostic only)"
    },
    {
      "ref": "C01 repair_requests",
      "text": "C01 repair_requests: numerator = records / rounds; denominator = - (counts); per trajectory and per improved cell; unit = repair generation."
    },
    {
      "ref": "C02 tokens",
      "text": "C02 tokens: numerator = token sums; denominator = generations (per-request means); reasoning tokens only over generations where the provider reports the field; unit = generation."
    },
    {
      "ref": "C03 repair_latency",
      "text": "C03 repair_latency: numerator = -; denominator = direct-mode generations; unit = generation."
    },
    {
      "ref": "C05 gain_per_effort",
      "text": "C05 gain_per_effort: numerator = improved cells; denominator = repair output tokens / requests of the variant; unit = variant x model."
    }
  ],
  "ci_note": null,
